{ Play what you have learned. }
1. d4 { [%csl Rd4][%cal Rd2d4] } 1... d5 { [%csl Gd5][%cal Gd7d5] } 2. c4 { [%csl Rc4][%cal Rc2c4] } 2... c6 { [%csl Gc6,Rd4,Rc4,Gd5][%cal Gc7c6] } 3. Nf3 { [%csl Rf3][%cal Rg1f3] } 3... Nf6 { [%csl Gf6][%cal Gg8f6] } 4. Nc3 { [%csl Rc3][%cal Rb1c3] } 4... e6 { This is the Semi-Slav. } { [%csl Ge6][%cal Ge7e6] } 5. e3 { This is the Meran Semi-Slav! White has to defend his pawn or else maybe we can take it and play b5, holding on to it. I will try to give you some ideas here, like how to develop the c8 bishop. } { [%csl Re3][%cal Re2e3,Yf1c4,Bd5c4] } *

[Event "The 💥 Semi-Slav! ✔: The Meran: Taking dxc4 at the right moment."]
[Date "2021.08.20"]
[Result "*"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ECO "D46"]
[Opening "Semi-Slav Defense: Chigorin Defense"]
[StudyName "The 💥 Semi-Slav! ✔"]
[ChapterName "The Meran: Taking dxc4 at the right moment."]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/ZIXAwbuB/dMvqMd6N"]
[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/heyucatchthis"]
[FEN "rnbqkb1r/pp3ppp/2p1pn2/3p4/2PP4/2N1PN2/PP3PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 0 5"]
[SetUp "1"]
[UTCDate "2021.08.20"]
[UTCTime "23:16:20"]
[Orientation "black"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ Black just played e3. Do we take on c4 now? Or is it better to develop the knight to d7? } { [%csl Re3][%cal Bb8d7,Re2e3,Bd5c4] }
5... Nbd7 { Yes! If we played dxc4, they could take back on c4 with tempo, while developing. We don't want to help white develop. We want to make sure the f1 bishop moves first, then take it. } { [%csl Gd7][%cal Gb8d7,Rd5c4,Rf1c4] } (5... dxc4? { No! This move is bad because after Bxc4 he got to develop his bishop while we were taking a pawn, not developing like white. } { [%csl Bc4][%cal Bf1c4] }) 6. Qc2 { Our opponent just responded with a smart queen move. Do we take now, or do we play Bd6? } { [%csl Rc2][%cal Rd1c2,Bd5c4,Bf8d6] } 6... Bd6 { Yes. We don't want to take on c4 unless the bishop moves first. } { [%csl Gd6][%cal Gf8d6,Rd5c4,Rf1c4] } (6... dxc4? { We want to wait for the bishop to move. } { [%csl Bc4][%cal Bf1c4] }) 7. Bd3 { How about now? } { [%csl Rd3][%cal Rf1d3,Bd5c4,Be8g8] } 7... dxc4 { Yes! We make the bishop move again. See, if we took earlier, white would not have to play Bd3. Because he did, he wasted some time. } { [%csl Gc4][%cal Rf1d3,Rd3c4] } (7... O-O { This move is good, as long as you will on c4 later. } { [%csl Gg8,Yd3][%cal Ge8g8,Bd5c4,Yc4d3] }) 8. Bxc4 { We still have a bad c8 bishop! Let's learn how to develop it. } { [%csl Rc4,Yc8][%cal Rd3c4] } *

