[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/heyucatchthis"]
[FEN "r1bqk2r/pp1n1ppp/2pbpn2/8/2BP4/2N1PN2/PPQ2PPP/R1B1K2R b KQkq - 0 8"]
[SetUp "1"]
[UTCDate "2021.08.20"]
[UTCTime "23:25:46"]
[Orientation "black"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ Black just took our c4 pawn. Play b5. } { [%csl Rc4][%cal Rd3c4,Bb7b5] }
8... b5 { This move forces the bishop back. Since now the b7 square is empty, our bishop can go there. } { [%csl Gb5][%cal Gb7b5,Bb5c4,Bc8b7] } 9. Bd3 { Follow our plan. } { [%csl Rd3][%cal Rc4d3,Bc8b7] } 9... Bb7 { Our position is still quite dormant, but soon we will wake it up! } { [%csl Gb7][%cal Gb7h1,Bc6c5,Gc8b7] } 10. O-O { The King } { [%csl Rg1,Ye8][%cal Re1g1] } 10... O-O 11. a3 { Right now, don't focus on the exact position, focus on the b7 bishop. We need to open the diagonal with c5, but then b5 would be hanging. Defend b5. } { [%csl Ra3][%cal Ra2a3] } 11... a6 { We are now ready to play c5. } { [%csl Ga6][%cal Ga7a6,Bc6c5] } 12. Kh1 { If white just sits around and does nothing, we can now open our bishops. } { [%cal Bc6c5] } 12... c5 { After c5, look how energetic our position is! We are ready for a full kingside attack. Our sleeping position has exploded, and now we are much better. } { [%csl Gc5][%cal Gc6c5,Bb7g2,Bd6h2,Bf6g4,Bd8h4] } *

