{ Let's say you are playing the Semi-Slav and you get to this position. Since we don't have a strong d5 pawn now, our opponent might take advantage of this. }
1. e4 { White plays e4, creating a strong center. Also, if white plays e5, they would deliver a nasty central pawn fork. We have to prevent this. If we don't want our opponent to play e5, we have to play e5 ourselves. } { [%csl Re4,Rd4][%cal Re3e4,Ye4e5,Ye5f6,Ye5d6,Be6e5] } 1... e5 { This move e5 has prevented e5 from white and also disrupts his center control. Now, we can play a6, taking on d4 at some point, and then c5 when our position wakes up. } { [%csl Ge5,Bb7,Bd6,Bf6,Bd8][%cal Ge6e5,Be5d4,Ba7a6,Bc6c5] } *

