{ This is a Semi-Slav game played by GM Anand and GM Aronian. We will see how well the opening can be used! }
1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. Nc3 e6 5. e3 Nbd7 6. Bd3 { [%cal Rf1d3] } 6... dxc4 { Anand takes so that the f1 bishop has to move twice. } { [%cal Rf1d3,Rd3c4,Gd5c4] } 7. Bxc4 b5 8. Bd3 Bd6 { [%cal Gd6h2] } 9. O-O O-O 10. Qc2 Bb7 { Preparing to activate it with c5. } { [%cal Gb7g2,Bc6c5] } 11. a3 Rc8 { [%cal Gc6c5] } 12. Ng5 c5! { A great pawn sacrifice } { [%csl Rh7,Yd3,Yc2,Yg5][%cal Yg5h7,Yc2h7] } 13. Nxh7 (13. Bxb5? { fails to } 13... cxd4! 14. exd4 h6 15. Nf3 (15. Nh3 Qc7 { The white king is getting destroyed. } { [%cal Gc7h2,Gb7g2,Gf6g4] }) 15... Bxf3 16. gxf3 Nd5 { and white has a lot of compensation for the pawn. } { [%csl Gd5,Gd6,Gd7,Gc8,Rf2,Rf3,Rh2] }) 13... Ng4 { Look at the amount of firepower black has. The rook on f8 does not matter if white is getting mated. } { [%csl Rf8][%cal Gd8h4,Gg4h2,Gb7g2,Gd6h2] } 14. f4 { [%csl Yf4][%cal Rd6h2] } (14. Nxf8?? { fails to } 14... Bxh2+ 15. Kh1 Qh4 { and there is no way to prevent mate. } { [%cal Gh4h1] }) 14... cxd4 15. exd4 Bc5!! { The bishop is for free. } 16. Be2? { is what Aronian played. This fails because of } (16. dxc5 Nxc5 { threatens to win the bishop. } { [%cal Gc5d3,Gd8d3] } 17. Bxb5?? { fails to } 17... Qd4+! 18. Kh1 Ne4 { and white has to sacrifice material to prevent mate. Look at how powerful black's attack is! } { [%cal Gd4g1,Gg4h2,Be4f2,Bb7g2] }) 16... Nde5!! { So much stuff is hanging! This is awesome play from Vishy. } { [%cal Gd4e5,Gd4c5] } 17. Bxg4 (17. fxe5? Qxd4+ 18. Kh1 Qg1+ { Smothered mate, 0-1 } 19. Rxg1 Nf2#) 17... Bxd4+ 18. Kh1 Nxg4 { The queen is coming and white is completely lost. } { [%cal Gd8h4] } 19. Nxf8 f5!! { [%cal Rc2h7] } (19... Qh4?? $10 { bringing the queen fails to } 20. Qh7+! { and black trades queens. }) 20. Ng6 Qf6 { Once the queen comes to the h-file, he can checkmate. } { [%cal Gf6h6] } 21. h3 Qxg6 22. Qe2 (22. hxg4 Qh6#) 22... Qh5 23. Qd3 Be3! $18 { 0-1 Black wins. } { A truly amazing game from the Semi-Slav. } 24. Bxe3 (24. Bxe3 Qxh3+ 25. Kg1 Qxg2#) 24... Qxh3+ 25. Kg1 Qxg2# 0-1
